title: "North Korean Forces Massacre in Jinju"
description_status: "This footage shows everyday scenes of U.S. forces, as well as the bodies of those massacred by North Korean forces in Jinju and wounded civilians."
description: "Shot list"
shotlist: "Shot List. Korean War, 25th Infantry Division, Jinju / 1950.9.25, 27, 30. #1 0:00 Soldiers assisting as a truck is moved onto a bypass road. Soldiers pushing the truck up onto the bypass. (Full shot / medium shot / close-up) 25th Infantry Division Commander Brigadier General George B. Bars directing traffic. (Medium shot) A truck passes. On the hill to the right, Brigadier General Bars is standing. #2 1:17 ROK forces unit, the Cacti Raiders, eating in a ditch. Tank crew inspecting an M-24 light tank that hit an anti-tank mine. (Medium shots) A few soldiers sitting on the ground. A radio set standing beside them. #3 2:23 Soldiers unloading ammunition from a destroyed M-24 light tank. (Close-up) The destroyed M-24. (Close-up) "Welcome US ARMY" written on the M-24. Soldiers resting near a bridge. (Medium shot / left to right) 89th Tank Battalion Lt. Colonel Durbin, 35th Infantry Regiment Colonel Henry Fisher, 25th Division Commander Major General William B. Kean looking at a map in a jeep. Outskirts of Jinju. (Medium shot) Colonel Fisher and Major General Kean. (Medium shot) 35th Regiment vehicles parked along the road. #4 4:33 Vehicles with soldiers crossing an emergency bridge built by the 65th Engineer Company (next to a wrecked bridge). Korean War, 25th Infantry Division, Jinju / 1950.9.25, 27, 30 (continued). #4 5:44 Two military personnel walking among the bodies of approximately 500 men, women, and children killed by North Korean forces. (Close-up) Several bodies. (Long shot) Bodies in a ditch. (Medium shot) A corpse bleeding from the head and face. (Close-up) Bound hands. Close-up, part of a body. #5 6:49 A medic administering first aid to a child. A medic wrapping a small child's body in bandages. (Close-up) The body of a dead woman. A Korean woman walking among the corpses to identify a loved one. #7:56 Many shots of the bodies. A U.S. soldier sitting on his heels looking at the corpses. Shaking his head. (Close-up) Two Korean women. One is sobbing. (Close-up) The sobbing woman. #9:02 25th Division Signal construction unit installing telephone lines for the 35th Division. Laying telephone lines through the village street. Laying telephone lines from a truck. (Close-up) A signal corps soldier carrying wire moving toward the camera. A man climbing a telephone pole."
